# Factory arguments

A free name in an `@` slot is not a hole and not a null. It is an argument
to the generated factory. Target must pass it; Construction does not build it.

`pen` appears first (and only once), so the factory is `SketchAssemblage.factory(pen: Pen)`.

## Schema

```
Pen = String/ink
Sketch = String/name @Pen
```

## Construction

```
[:Sketch "star" pen]
```

## Methods

```
Sketch::caption = { name.concat(" drawn in ").concat(pen.ink) }
```

## Target

```
%terminal

%requires
Pen

%main
public static function main():Void {
    var pen = new Pen("blue");
    var s = SketchAssemblage.factory(pen);
    trace(s.caption());
}
```
